__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
pgdata/
# Eval worksheets hold real colleague speech; they live outside the
# repo (the builder enforces it) -- this is the second line of defence.
*attribution*.json
task-ledger-eval/
# Raw meeting transcripts are real colleague speech, named and timestamped.
# transcript_ingest.py reads them from wherever they are; nothing about the
# workflow needs them inside the repo, so make committing one take effort.
transcript*.txt
*transcript*raw*.txt
*_raw.txt

# A Copilot claims export is real meeting speech too, and increasingly so:
# the prompt now demands a VERBATIM quote per claim, because a quote we can
# find in the transcript is what lifts the confidence cap. So the export is
# not a summary of what was said, it is a file of sentences colleagues
# actually spoke, with their names against them.
#
# Only 'copilot_claims_raw.txt' was covered, by the generic *_raw.txt rule
# above -- one character off that name and the file was committable. Named
# by extension so the tracked .py, .md and .sql keep their names.
copilot*claims*.txt
copilot*claims*.json
claims*.txt
claims*.json
*_claims.txt
*_claims.json
# Status reports are a person's own task list, named and dated -- the
# same class as transcripts, fenced the same way. They are ingested
# from wherever they live; nothing needs them inside the repo.
*status*.txt
